course: dictionary
lesson: 9561
title: Strabismus: the medical word for a squint
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: A new word can look scary, but its context often gives you the meaning. «A squint, or strabismus, is when the eyes don't line up.» The words «or» and «is when» tell you that squint and strabismus mean the same thing.
explain: Strabismus is the medical name for a squint. It happens when a person's two eyes do not point in the same direction at the same time, so one eye may turn in, out, up or down.
explain: Doctors and eye helpers use this word most. «Orthoptists, eye workers who help with squints and lazy eyes, may suggest glasses, patches or an operation.» The words after the comma explain who orthoptists are, so you do not need to look them up.
explain: In everyday talk, people in the UK say «squint». «Crossed eyes» and «lazy eye» are informal phrases, but they are not exactly the same as strabismus, so use the medical or everyday word when you write.
fact: Strabismus means a squint: the eyes do not point in the same direction at the same time.
fact: Strabismus is a medical word, so doctors and eye workers use it most.
fact: The two eyes work together to help us see depth, so a squint can affect how we judge distance.
fact: Treatments can include glasses, an eye patch, eye exercises or a small operation.
fact: It is a common condition, and nobody should tease anyone about it.
exercise: «A squint, or strabismus, is when the eyes don't line up.» What does strabismus mean? | *A squint, when the two eyes do not point the same way | Wearing sunglasses all day | A type of eye drop | A cold affecting the eyes
exercise: Which everyday word in the UK means the same as strabismus? | Lazy eye | *Squint | Blink | Crossed eyes
exercise: «Orthoptists, eye workers who help with squints and lazy eyes, may suggest glasses, patches or an operation.» Who are orthoptists? | People who sell sunglasses in shops | *Eye workers who help with squints and lazy eyes | Doctors who only give out sweets | Teachers who teach reading
test: When a person has strabismus, what happens with their eyes? | They can see nothing at all | Both eyes look at the same spot at the same time | *Their two eyes do not point in the same direction at the same time | Their eyes change colour in the dark
test: Why should nobody tease a child who has strabismus? | Because it is catching | Because they must wear an eye patch in class | Because it is a dangerous illness | *Because it is a common condition, and teasing is unkind
exam: Which word is the best everyday match for strabismus? | Crossed eyes | *Squint | Lazy eye | Dry eyes
